{"type":"llm_response","timestamp":"2026-04-08T07:55:03.651Z","data":{"turn":162,"content":"{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Rz18V7eoJmgB3YwopfBPtq\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"save-deliverable --type INJECTION_QUEUE --content '{\\n  \\\"vulnerabilities\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"ID\\\": \\\"INJ-VULN-01\\\",\\n      \\\"vulnerability_type\\\": \\\"SQLi\\\",\\n      \\\"externally_exploitable\\\": true,\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"req.query.search — GET /api/users?search= (users.controller.js:7)\\\",\\n      \\\"combined_sources\\\": \\\"Single source: req.query.search\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"users.routes.js:10 (public route, no auth) → users.controller.js:7 (destructure) → users.controller.js:10 (pass to service) → users.service.js:33 (ILIKE concat sink)\\\",\\n      \\\"sink_call\\\": \\\"src/users/users.service.js:33 and :37-38 — db.raw() with template-literal-built SQL string\\\",\\n      \\\"slot_type\\\": \\\"SQL-like\\\",\\n      \\\"sanitization_observed\\\": \\\"None\\\",\\n      \\\"concat_occurrences\\\": \\\"users.service.js:33 — template literal `%${search}%` embedded directly into query string before db.raw() call; users.service.js:37 — same tainted query string reused in countQuery via subquery\\\",\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"vulnerable\\\",\\n      \\\"mismatch_reason\\\": \\\"Template literal embeds raw user input into the SQL ILIKE clause. The params array passed to db.raw() contains only limit/offset — search is NOT bound as a parameter. The tainted string is already baked into the SQL command text at the time db.raw() is called.\\\",\\n      \\\"witness_payload\\\": \\\"'\\\"'\\\"' OR 1=1--\\\",\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Endpoint is fully public (no authentication middleware on users.routes.js:10). Error responses return {error: \\\\\\\"Failed to fetch users\\\\\\\"} — no verbose DB error to caller, suggesting blind injection techniques. PostgreSQL 15 target. Also injectable via: pg_sleep(5) for time-based, UNION SELECT for schema enumeration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"ID\\\": \\\"INJ-VULN-02\\\",\\n      \\\"vulnerability_type\\\": \\\"SQLi\\\",\\n      \\\"externally_exploitable\\\": true,\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"req.query.search — GET /api/admin/users?search= (admin.controller.js:16)\\\",\\n      \\\"combined_sources\\\": \\\"Single source: req.query.search\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"admin.routes.js:15 (requireAdmin guard — bypassable via forged JWT) → admin.controller.js:16 (destructure) → admin.controller.js:19 (pass to service) → admin.service.js:66 (whereRaw concat sink)\\\",\\n      \\\"sink_call\\\": \\\"src/admin/admin.service.js:66 — Knex whereRaw() with + string concatenation\\\",\\n      \\\"slot_type\\\": \\\"SQL-like\\\",\\n      \\\"sanitization_observed\\\": \\\"None\\\",\\n      \\\"concat_occurrences\\\": \\\"admin.service.js:66 — string + concatenation: \\\\\\\"display_name ILIKE \\\\\\\\'%\\\\\\\" + search + \\\\\\\"%\\\\\\\\' OR email ILIKE \\\\\\\\'%\\\\\\\" + search + \\\\\\\"%\\\\\\\\'\\\\\\\" passed directly to whereRaw()\\\",\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"vulnerable\\\",\\n      \\\"mismatch_reason\\\": \\\"whereRaw() receives a fully-formed SQL fragment built by + concatenation. Knex has no opportunity to bind search as a parameter — the value is structurally embedded in the SQL before Knex processes it.\\\",\\n      \\\"witness_payload\\\": \\\"'\\\"'\\\"' OR pg_sleep(5)--\\\",\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Requires admin role. JWT secret is hardcoded as hireflow2024api (src/config/index.js:29, HS256). Forge token: {id: any, email: any, role: admin} signed with that secret to bypass requireAdmin. Two query executions occur on the same tainted string: count query (line 70) and paginated result query (line 79-82). PostgreSQL 15 target.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"ID\\\": \\\"INJ-VULN-03\\\",\\n      \\\"vulnerability_type\\\": \\\"SQLi\\\",\\n      \\\"externally_exploitable\\\": true,\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"req.query.tag_filter — GET /api/gigs?tag_filter= (gigs.controller.js:10)\\\",\\n      \\\"combined_sources\\\": \\\"Single source: req.query.tag_filter\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"gigs.routes.js:8 (public, optionalAuth) → gigs.controller.js:10 (pass req.query to service) → gigs.service.js:19 (destructure tag_filter) → gigs.service.js:41-46 (MongoDB $where template literal sink)\\\",\\n      \\\"sink_call\\\": \\\"src/gigs/gigs.service.js:41-46 — MongoDB $where operator with template literal JavaScript function body\\\",\\n      \\\"slot_type\\\": \\\"TEMPLATE-expression\\\",\\n      \\\"sanitization_observed\\\": \\\"None\\\",\\n      \\\"concat_occurrences\\\": \\\"gigs.service.js:44 — template literal `return ${tag_filter};` embeds user input as executable JavaScript inside $where function body\\\",\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"vulnerable\\\",\\n      \\\"mismatch_reason\\\": \\\"tag_filter is embedded verbatim as the return expression of a MongoDB $where JavaScript function. Any valid JavaScript expression is accepted, enabling arbitrary logic (e.g., always-true bypass, db collection access). No sanitization, escaping, or allowlist applied.\\\",\\n      \\\"witness_payload\\\": \\\"true || (function(){return true;})()\\\",\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"med\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"MongoDB 7 disables $where / javascriptEnabled by default. Verify mongod.conf for javascriptEnabled:true before investing exploitation resources. If disabled, the code is structurally vulnerable but the $where operator will be rejected at the MongoDB layer with an error. All other gig filter params (category, tags, min_price, max_price, sort, page, limit) are SAFE — see Section 5 of the analysis report.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"ID\\\": \\\"INJ-VULN-04\\\",\\n      \\\"vulnerability_type\\\": \\\"SQLi\\\",\\n      \\\"externally_exploitable\\\": true,\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"req.query.usernames (comma-separated string, split to array) — GET /api/admin/reports/activity?usernames= (admin.controller.js:244,251)\\\",\\n      \\\"combined_sources\\\": \\\"Single source: req.query.usernames (split on comma at controller level)\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"admin.routes.js:25 (requireAdmin — bypassable via forged JWT) → admin.controller.js:244 (extract) → admin.controller.js:251 (split+trim only) → admin.service.js:360 (quote-wrap each element) → admin.service.js:361 (JSON string concat) → admin.service.js:362 (JSON.parse → live query object) → admin.service.js:371 (ActivityLog.find sink)\\\",\\n      \\\"sink_call\\\": \\\"src/admin/admin.service.js:361-362 — manual JSON string construction followed by JSON.parse(); src/admin/admin.service.js:371 — ActivityLog.find(filter)\\\",\\n      \\\"slot_type\\\": \\\"DESERIALIZE-object\\\",\\n      \\\"sanitization_observed\\\": \\\"None (quote-wrapping with double-quotes at line 360 provides no protection — the value itself can contain unescaped double-quote characters)\\\",\\n      \\\"concat_occurrences\\\": \\\"admin.service.js:360 — '\\\\\\\"' + u + '\\\\\\\"' (no JSON escaping of u); admin.service.js:361 — userFilter string concatenated into JSON template\\\",\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"vulnerable\\\",\\n      \\\"mismatch_reason\\\": \\\"The quote-wrapping at line 360 assumes username values will not contain double-quote characters. An attacker injects a username with embedded quotes and MongoDB operators that break out of the $in array and inject arbitrary query operators. JSON.parse() at line 362 materializes the attacker-controlled structure as a live MongoDB filter object.\\\",\\n      \\\"witness_payload\\\": \\\"alice\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$or\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"metadata.username\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"$ne\\\\\\\":null}}],\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"a\\\",\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"Requires admin role. Bypass via forged JWT with secret hireflow2024api. ActivityLog model stores action, resource_type, resource_id, description, metadata (Mixed type), ip_address, user_agent fields — operator injection can filter/expose all log entries. The $in array element injection turns into full query object manipulation after JSON.parse.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"ID\\\": \\\"INJ-VULN-05\\\",\\n      \\\"vulnerability_type\\\": \\\"SSTI\\\",\\n      \\\"externally_exploitable\\\": true,\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"req.body.display_name via PUT /api/users/:id (stored); req.body.title via POST/PUT /api/contracts/:id/milestones (stored). Triggered via GET /api/contracts/:id/invoice.\\\",\\n      \\\"combined_sources\\\": \\\"Primary: users.display_name (stored) | Secondary: milestones.title (stored) | Both fetched at contracts.service.js:431-447\\\",\\n      \\\"path\\\": \\\"[Store] PUT /api/users/:id → users.service.js:111-134 updateProfile() → DB users.display_name (no content validation) | [Trigger] GET /api/contracts/:id/invoice → contracts.controller.js:222 → contracts.service.js:431-447 generateInvoice() → pdf.js:61,74 buildInvoiceHTML() template literals → pdf.js:15-16 page.setContent() Chromium render\\\",\\n      \\\"sink_call\\\": \\\"src/utils/pdf.js:61 — ${data.clientName} in HTML template; src/utils/pdf.js:74 — ${item.description} in HTML template; src/utils/pdf.js:15-16 — puppeteer page.setContent(html)\\\",\\n      \\\"slot_type\\\": \\\"TEMPLATE-expression\\\",\\n      \\\"sanitization_observed\\\": \\\"None at any stage: storage (users.service.js:111-134 — field accepted verbatim), retrieval (contracts.service.js:442,447 — no escaping), or template construction (pdf.js:61,74 — no HTML encoding)\\\",\\n      \\\"concat_occurrences\\\": \\\"pdf.js:61 — `${data.clientName}` (post-storage, no sanitization ever applied); pdf.js:74 — `${item.description}`; also pdf.js:55 — `${data.invoiceNumber}`, pdf.js:56 — `${data.date}` (lower risk as system-generated)\\\",\\n      \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"vulnerable\\\",\\n      \\\"mismatch_reason\\\": \\\"HTML